    {
      "description": "Shows how busy your computer’s brain (CPU) is. Higher values mean more work. If it stays high (>85%) for several minutes, apps may lag. Good for spotting heavy background tasks. Missing series are unavailable, not zero. Optional hardware, unmounted disks, stopped VMs and inactive collectors may have no samples.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "max": 100,
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 70
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 85
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percent",
          "noValue": "Unavailable"
        }
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "options": {
        "graphMode": "area",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "((1 - avg(rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{mode=\"idle\"}[5m])) by (instance)) * 100)",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "title": "CPU %",
      "type": "stat",
      "id": 6
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows how much RAM is in use. Higher values mean less free memory for new apps. Sustained high memory usage can cause slowdowns and app switching delays. Missing series are unavailable, not zero. Optional hardware, unmounted disks, stopped VMs and inactive collectors may have no samples.",
